# Crucible web app — every variable is optional.
# With none of them set, the app runs entirely on fixture data and needs no
# backend, no wallet and no network access. That is the default and it is
# deliberate: the demo must never depend on another service being up.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Orchestrator (services/orchestrator) — INTERFACES.md §5
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset  → mock mode: jobs are simulated in memory, passports come from fixtures.
# Set    → live mode: every call in src/lib/api.ts hits this base URL.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CRUCIBLE_API_URL=http://localhost:8787

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Passport contract (contracts/) — INTERFACES.md §4
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployed addresses of Passport.sol, per network. Until these are set, the
# passport page labels its contract address as a placeholder rather than linking
# to an explorer page that does not exist. They are separate because a passport
# must show the contract for ITS network — a mainnet address next to testnet
# provenance would misdirect anyone trying to verify it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PASSPORT_ADDRESS_MAINNET=0x...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PASSPORT_ADDRESS_TESTNET=0x...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wallet connection
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A WalletConnect Cloud project id (https://cloud.reown.com). Without it the app
# falls back to injected wallets only — MetaMask, Rabby, and anything else that
# injects window.ethereum. It does NOT initialise WalletConnect with a
# placeholder id, because that breaks the connect modal at runtime.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=
